    "result_text": "All tests green (there's a single test class, `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes along with a clean compile).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation following the codebase's established \"one small policy class per business rule\" pattern, keeping structural impact low.\n\n**New behaviour as a small, cohesive unit:**\n- `service/OwnerAgeBandPolicy.java` \u2014 a new self-contained policy (CC ~3, zero surrounding class complexity) that derives `MINOR` / `ADULT` / `SENIOR` from `birthDate` against `registrationDate`, returning `null` when no `birthDate` is present \u2014 mirroring `OwnerMembershipLevelPolicy` and the other policies.\n\n**Minimal edits to existing units:**\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 one `@Mapping` expression line wiring `ageBand`, exactly like the sibling derived fields.\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 a `birthDate` column plus a trivial getter/setter (CC 1 each); MapStruct maps `birthDate` in and out automatically by name.\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 `birthDate` added to `OwnerFields` (input) and `ageBand` to `Owner` (read-only output), so the generated DTOs carry both.\n\n**Schema (hsqldb is the test DB, `ddl-auto=none`):**\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` \u2014 added `birth_date DATE`.\n- `db/hsqldb/data.sql` \u2014 appended a trailing `NULL` to the 10 positional owner seed inserts.\n\nI deliberately left the h2/postgres/mysql schemas untouched: they already omit `postcode`/`namesake_count` (h2 relies on `ddl-auto=update`), so matching that precedent avoids touching extra files. No existing method grew in complexity \u2014 the change is a new class plus one-line hooks.",
